@node User Options
@subsection User Options
@cindex user options

@defvr {User Option} beads-executable
Path to the @command{bd} executable.  Defaults to @code{"bd"}, found on
@env{PATH}.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-actor
The actor name recorded in the audit trail.  Defaults to the git
@code{user.name} or @env{USER}.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-remote-search-path
Directories probed for programs on a remote host when
@code{tramp-remote-path} misses (Guix, Nix, @file{~/.local/bin}, and
@file{~/bin} by default).  Also prepended to the @env{PATH} of remote
commands.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-remote-transport
@code{ssh} (the default): asynchronous @command{bd} on an ssh-family
store runs as a local @command{ssh -T} pipe.  @code{tramp}: use TRAMP's
@code{make-process}.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-remote-ssh-options
The ssh options (ControlMaster, ControlPersist) of the pipe processes.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-remote-ssh-control-path
The ControlPath of those pipe processes.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-show-async
When show buffers fetch asynchronously: @code{remote} (the default),
@code{t}, or @code{nil}.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-show-async-timeout
The number of seconds an asynchronous show fetch may take before it is
abandoned.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-dashboard-section-limit
The number of rows shown per dashboard section; @code{nil} disables the
cap.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-command-async-max-concurrent
The global concurrency cap for asynchronous commands, or @code{auto} to
size it to the machine.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-issue-id-prefixes
Extra issue-id prefixes matched by the shared issue-id regular
expression.  @code{nil} uses the defaults.
@end defvr

@defvr {User Option} beads-issue-id-regexp
The regular expression that matches an issue id anywhere in a buffer.
@end defvr

Use @kbd{M-x customize-group @key{RET} beads} for the full option
browser.  The per-project configuration that is not a user option is in
@ref{Configuration}.

@node Faces
@subsection Faces
@cindex faces

Beads.el defines faces for issue status, priority, type, and other UI
elements.  Customize the @code{beads} and @code{beads-epic-status} face
groups to adjust colors.  The status and priority faces are applied by
the list and board renderers; they inherit from the corresponding
@code{font-lock} and @code{mode-line} faces so a theme overrides them
consistently.

@node Plumbing
@section Plumbing
@cindex plumbing

This section is for contributors.  It describes how the command layer is
built and where to change it.

@menu
* EIEIO Command Classes::
* Execution Contract::
* The Command Bridge Protocol::
@end menu

@node EIEIO Command Classes
@subsection EIEIO Command Classes
@cindex EIEIO command classes
@cindex beads-defcommand

Every @command{bd} subcommand is represented as an EIEIO class defined
with the @code{beads-defcommand} macro.  A single class definition
generates:

@enumerate
@item
an EIEIO class with typed slots,
@item
CLI argument serialization (@code{beads-command-line}),
@item
an auto-generated transient menu derived from slot metadata, and
@item
a result type declaration that drives JSON parsing into
@code{beads-types.el} objects.
@end enumerate

@defmac beads-defcommand name superclass slots &rest options
Define a command class @var{name} with @var{slots}, deriving the CLI
serialization, transient menu, and result type from the slot metadata.
@end defmac

The class hierarchy is @code{beads-command} (abstract) →
@code{beads-command-global-options} (adds @code{--actor}, @code{--db},
@code{--json}) → concrete commands.

Macro keywords include @code{:cli-command} (override the subcommand
string), @code{:result} (for example @code{beads-issue} or
@code{(list-of beads-issue)}), @code{:json nil} for commands without
JSON (doctor, init), and @code{:transient} (@code{t} to auto-generate,
@code{nil} for none, @code{:manual} when a hand-written prefix follows in
the same file).  The transient name is the class name with
@code{-command-} stripped, so @code{beads-command-close} becomes
@code{beads-close}.

Slot metadata drives both the CLI and the UI: a single slot definition
carries CLI properties (@code{:long-option}, @code{:short-option},
@code{:option-type}, @code{:positional}), transient properties
(@code{:class}, @code{:reader}, @code{:choices}, @code{:group},
@code{:level}), and validation (@code{:required}, @code{:validator}).

@node Execution Contract
@subsection Execution Contract
@cindex execution contract

Command objects are never mutated; execution clones them.  Three generics
dispatch on the command.

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-execute (command)
Synchronously run COMMAND.  Forces @code{--json}, runs @command{bd},
parses through @code{beads-from-json}, and returns typed domain objects
(or a raw string when @code{:json nil}).  Unit tests mock this.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-execute-interactive (command)
The entry point for transient suffixes.  The default runs COMMAND in a
@code{compilation-mode} buffer; commands override it to show or refresh a
buffer.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-execute-async (command &key on-success on-error queue cache-key)
Run COMMAND without blocking, calling ON-SUCCESS or ON-ERROR.  A non-nil
QUEUE applies the global concurrency cap and CACHE-KEY coalesces
identical concurrent requests.  The board, eldoc, and list loaders use
this path.
@end deftypefn

Errors signal @code{beads-validation-error}, @code{beads-command-error},
or @code{beads-json-parse-error}; the hierarchy lives in
@code{beads-error.el}.

@node The Command Bridge Protocol
@subsection The Command Bridge Protocol
@cindex command bridge protocol
@cindex extension contract

@code{beads-defcommand} and @code{beads-meta-define-transient} generate
menus whose execute and preview suffixes call exactly three generic
functions.  These are the supported extension contract for a consumer
package that defines its own command base class:

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-validate (command)
Return an error string (or a list of them) when COMMAND is invalid, or
nil when it is valid.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-execute-interactive (command)
Run COMMAND and present the result.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-command-preview (command)
Return the command line that would run, without running it.
@end deftypefn

@lisp
(defclass my-command (beads-command-global-options) ()
  :abstract t
  :documentation "Base class for my-tool commands.")

(cl-defmethod beads-command-validate ((cmd my-command)) ...)
(cl-defmethod beads-command-execute-interactive ((cmd my-command)) ...)
(cl-defmethod beads-command-preview ((cmd my-command)) ...)
@end lisp

@node Extending beads.el
@section Extending beads.el
@anchor{extending}
@cindex extending
@cindex library reuse

beads.el is meant to be reused as a library.  The entry points below are
supported and their signatures are kept stable; prefer them over the
private (@code{beads--}) symbols, which may change without notice.

@menu
* Macro-Expansion Helpers::
* Section Buffers and Mode Inheritance::
* Thing Motion::
* Reusable Pagination::
@end menu

@node Macro-Expansion Helpers
@subsection Macro-Expansion Helpers
@cindex macro-expansion helpers

The pure helpers @code{beads-defcommand} uses at macro-expansion time are
public.

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-meta-extract-option (keyword options)
Pull KEYWORD's value out of a @code{defclass} OPTIONS plist.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-meta-derive-transient-name (class-name)
Derive a transient name from CLASS-NAME.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-meta-first-sentence (string)
Return the first sentence of STRING, for a transient short documentation
string.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-meta-current-feature-name ()
Return the feature name of the file being processed, for autoload forms.
@end deftypefn

@node Section Buffers and Mode Inheritance
@subsection Section Buffers and Mode Inheritance
@cindex section buffers
@cindex mode inheritance

Derive a major mode from @code{beads-section-mode} and parent its keymap.

@lisp
(defvar-keymap my-section-mode-map
  :parent beads-section-mode-map
  "RET" #'my-visit-thing-at-point)

(define-derived-mode my-section-mode beads-section-mode "My"
  "Major mode for my-tool section buffers."
  :interactive nil)
@end lisp

@node Thing Motion
@subsection Thing Motion
@cindex thing motion
@cindex beads-thing

A @dfn{thing} is a run of text carrying the @code{beads-thing} text
property; in a @code{tabulated-list-mode} buffer every row is one.  The
value is a toggle function, a plist @code{( :kind KIND :toggle FN )}, or
any other non-nil value.

@lisp
(beads-thing-define-keys my-section-mode-map) ; TAB, S-TAB, SPC, DEL/S-SPC

(beads-thing-propertize "Agents  3 running"
                        (list :kind 'section :toggle #'my-fold))
(add-hook 'beads-thing-toggle-functions #'my-toggle-drawer nil t)
@end lisp

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-thing-forward (&optional count)
Move to the next thing, wrapping at the end.  Bound to @kbd{TAB}.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-thing-backward (&optional count)
Move to the previous thing, wrapping at the beginning.  Bound to
@kbd{S-TAB}.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-thing-toggle ()
Call the thing's own toggle, then the buffer-local
@code{beads-thing-toggle-functions}, then push the button at point for
kinds @code{section} and @code{fold}.  Bound to @kbd{SPC}.
@end deftypefn

@defvr {Variable} beads-thing-toggle-functions
Buffer-local hook run by @code{beads-thing-toggle} after the thing's own
toggle.
@end defvr

@node Reusable Pagination
@subsection Reusable Pagination
@cindex pagination
@cindex beads-pager

@code{beads-pager} exposes a pure, buffer-agnostic pagination core.

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-pager-window-page-size (&optional window)
Return the number of rows that fit WINDOW, with a floor of five.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-pager-page-count (total page-size)
Return the number of pages for TOTAL rows.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-pager-page-bounds (page page-size total)
Return the @code{(START . END)} indices of PAGE, clamped to TOTAL.
@end deftypefn

@deftypefn {Emacs Lisp Function} {} beads-pager-slice (entries page page-size)
Return the sublist of ENTRIES for PAGE.
@end deftypefn

These read no buffer-local state; @code{beads-pager-mode} is built on the
same core.

@node Building and Installing with Autotools
@section Building and Installing with Autotools
@anchor{building}
@cindex autotools
@cindex building
@cindex installing

beads.el is a GNU-standard Autotools project.  The build has no C
components, so it uses Automake's @code{foreign} strictness and does not
call @code{AC_PROG_CC}; it byte-compiles Elisp and builds the Texinfo
manual.

@menu
* Prerequisites::
* Bootstrapping and Configuring::
* Building Testing and Installing::
* Building the Manual::
* Guix Development Environment::
@end menu

@node Prerequisites
@subsection Prerequisites
@cindex build prerequisites

Building from a checkout needs Emacs 29.1 or newer, Autoconf, Automake,
and @command{makeinfo} (from Texinfo) for the manual.  The runtime Elisp
dependencies @code{transient} and @code{vui} must be resolvable, either
from the ambient @env{EMACSLOADPATH} or with @option{--with-} flags.
@command{bd}, @command{dolt}, and @command{graphviz} are optional: they
are detected for the @code{:integration} test suite and can be disabled
with @option{--with-bd=no} and friends.

@node Bootstrapping and Configuring
@subsection Bootstrapping and Configuring
@cindex autogen
@cindex configure

From a fresh checkout, generate the configure script and run it.

@example
./autogen.sh
./configure
@end example

@command{configure} locates Emacs (failing with a clear message when it
is missing) and the optional CLI tools.  Useful options:

@table @option
@item --with-emacs=PATH
Use a specific Emacs executable instead of searching @env{PATH}.
@item --with-transient=DIR
@itemx --with-vui=DIR
Add DIR to the load path for the runtime dependency.
@item --with-bd=PATH
@itemx --with-dolt=PATH
@itemx --with-graphviz=PATH
Name an optional CLI tool, or pass @code{no} to disable it.
@item --with-lispdir=DIR
Install Elisp into DIR instead of the default site-lisp directory.
@end table

If @option{--with-transient}/@option{--with-vui} are omitted, the
ambient @env{EMACSLOADPATH} is used unchanged; that is the Guix path.

@node Building Testing and Installing
@subsection Building, Testing, and Installing
@cindex make targets

@table @code
@item make
Byte-compile every @file{lisp/*.el} with warnings as errors, then
generate @file{lisp/beads-autoloads.el}.  A byte-compile warning fails
the build.
@item make check
Run the ERT test suite.  The @command{bd}/@command{dolt}/@command{graphviz}
conditionals decide how much of the @code{:integration} suite runs;
@code{EMACS_TEST_JUNIT_REPORT} selects the JUnit output.
@item make lint
Run byte-compile warnings-as-errors plus the package-lint checks through
@file{scripts/lint}, with no Eldev dependency.
@item make install
Install @file{*.el}, @file{*.elc}, the generated autoloads, and
@file{beads.info} into @code{lispdir} and @code{infodir}, and run
@command{install-info} so @kbd{C-h i} finds the manual.
@item make dist
Build the distribution tarball, including the Texinfo sources, the
manual images, @file{lisp/}, @file{docs/*.md}, and @file{guix.scm}.
@item make clean
Remove the byte-compiled files, the generated autoloads, and the built
manual.
@end table

A clean extraction of the @command{make dist} tarball must build and pass
@command{make check} with @command{./configure && make}.

@node Building the Manual
@subsection Building the Manual
@cindex building the manual
@cindex makeinfo

@table @code
@item make info
Build @file{doc/beads.info} from @file{doc/beads.texi}.
@item make html
Build the self-contained HTML manual under @file{doc/}.
@item make pdf
Build the PDF manual with @command{texi2pdf}.
@end table

@file{doc/beads.texi} is the only manual source; it @code{@@include}s one
Texinfo chapter file per task area (@pxref{The Dispatch and Maintenance
Menus} for where those chapters are).  @command{makeinfo} must report no
missing-node or undefined-reference warnings.

@node Guix Development Environment
@subsection Guix Development Environment
@cindex Guix

The repository ships a @file{guix.scm} describing the Autotools build.
Use it for a development shell with Emacs, the Elisp dependencies, and
the optional CLI tools on @env{PATH}:

@example
guix shell -D -f guix.scm
@end example

@code{guix build -f guix.scm} builds the package through the Autotools
flow.  The Guix package provides the Elisp dependencies through
@env{EMACSLOADPATH}, so no @option{--with-} flags are needed.

@node Linting and Documentation Drift
@section Linting and Documentation Drift
@anchor{linting}
@cindex linting
@cindex documentation drift
@cindex dispatch-docs

Quality gates and generated documentation are checked without Eldev.

@table @asis
@item Byte-compile and package lint
@code{make lint} runs byte-compile warnings-as-errors and the
@file{scripts/lint} wrapper, which invokes @code{package-lint} and the
byte-compiler under plain Emacs.
@item Dispatch and key reference
@code{scripts/dispatch-docs --check} fails when the hand-written
transient menus disagree with the generated Markdown in
@file{docs/dispatch-reference.md} and the README dispatch table.
Regenerate them with @code{scripts/dispatch-docs --write} after changing
a menu (@pxref{Command and Key Reference}).
@item Key registry
@file{lisp/test/beads-key-registry-test.el} asserts the effective
binding of every contract key in @file{docs/key-registry.md}, so a parent
keymap cannot silently re-point a key.
@end table

Run the same commands CI runs:

@example
./configure && make && make check && make lint
scripts/dispatch-docs --check
@end example

@node Contributing
@section Contributing
@anchor{contributing}
@cindex contributing

Contributions follow the conventions in @file{AGENTS.md}.  The
essentials:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Public API} uses the @code{beads-} prefix; @strong{internal} code
uses @code{beads--} and may change without notice.
@item
Every @command{bd} subcommand gets its own
@file{beads-command-<name>.el} file and a @code{beads-defcommand} class
(@pxref{EIEIO Command Classes}).
@item
Every EIEIO class and every slot carries a @code{:documentation} string.
@item
Menus are defined with @code{beads-define-prefix} /
@code{beads-define-group}, never bare @code{transient-define-prefix}, so
every suffix runs in the directory the menu was opened for.
@item
Tests live in @file{lisp/test/} as @file{<module>-test.el}, and every
@code{ert-deftest} carries a @code{:unit}, @code{:integration}, or
@code{:live} tag.
@end itemize

Add a user-visible or API-breaking change to the @file{NEWS.md}
@strong{Unreleased} section, and regenerate any generated documentation
(@pxref{Linting and Documentation Drift}) before opening a pull request.
Run @command{make}, @command{make check}, and @command{make lint} first.

@node Troubleshooting
@section Troubleshooting
@anchor{troubleshooting}
@cindex troubleshooting

@table @asis
@item @command{bd} not found
Set @code{beads-executable} to the absolute path of the program, or put
it on @env{PATH}.
@item Version skew between beads.el and @command{bd}
Run @kbd{M-x beads-version} and include the output in a bug report.  The
command surface must match the @command{bd} version.
@item Remote commands fail to authenticate
The ssh pipe runs in BatchMode, so interactive password prompts cannot
appear.  Use a key or a running ssh agent.
@item A remote view hangs
The first contact with a host resolves the project root synchronously;
raise @code{beads-remote-sync-timeout} for a slow host, or open the view
with an explicit @code{:directory} (@pxref{Store Scoping}).
@item Byte-compile or lint failures
Warnings are errors; treat them as real and fix the offending source
rather than disabling the gate.
@item Documentation drift
Run @command{scripts/dispatch-docs --write} after changing a menu, then
rebuild the manual (@pxref{Linting and Documentation Drift}).
@end table

